# packet-flood-advert - an advert heard as a flood
# Route F, no transport codes, no path: the common case, and a score the formula clamps at 1 (1000).
#
# Written by hand from the observer firmware's source, agessaman/MeshCore observer-firmware @ d664d89df66bdacc1319900a2e2d152fa31b9dc9,
# and MeshCore at this firmware's pin, meshcore-dev/MeshCore @ d92964352441e53b93e8667b802e04f6e072b39e (companion-v1.17.1). Each field, and where it came from:
#   timestamp    MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:288-307  "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S" of gmtime, then ".%06ld+00:00" of the microseconds
#   hash         MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:543-547  Packet::calculatePacketHash as 16 uppercase hex (bytesToHex :606-622);
#                src/Packet.cpp:41-50 at the pin: SHA-256 of the payload type byte, then for a TRACE the two bytes of
#                path_len (a uint16_t, little-endian), then the payload; the first eight bytes of the digest. Computed
#                here with Python's hashlib over exactly those bytes
#   origin       MQTTBridge.cpp:38-47            mqtt.origin, else the node's name; here the fallback this firmware uses
#   type         MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:300      "PACKET"
#   direction    MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:556      "rx"
#   time, date   MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:521-532  "%H:%M:%S" and "%d/%m/%Y" of the same gmtime
#   len          MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:558, MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:293,304  the radio frame's length, as a string
#   packet_type  MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:540, MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:294,305  Packet::getPayloadType, as a string
#   route        MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:541,597-604  "D" when Packet::isRouteDirect (Packet.h:65: route 2 or 3), else "F"
#   payload_len  MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:560, MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:295,307  Packet::payload_len, as a string
#   raw          MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:534-537  the whole frame, uppercase hex
#   origin_id    examples/simple_repeater/MyMesh.cpp:1222-1226  the public key, Utils::toHex (uppercase at the pin, Utils.cpp:174-184)
#   SNR          MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:311-317  "%.1f" of the radio's SNR
#   RSSI         MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:318-321  "%d" of the RSSI, which arrives as a float through an int parameter (truncated)
#   score        MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:322-325  "%d" of (int)(score * 1000); score is RadioLibWrapper::packetScoreInt(snr, sf, len),
#                RadioLibWrappers.cpp:221-239 at the pin, computed here in the same float/double steps
#   path         MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:328-342 with MQTTMessageBuilder.cpp:551  only on a direct route with hops: one
#                lowercase hex token per hop, hashSize bytes each, at most four
# The field order is the order buildPacketMessage fills its document (MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:297-342).
#
# The frame: header 0x11 (version 0, type 4, route 1), path_len 0x00 (hash size 1, 0 hop(s)), 30 payload byte(s).
